{
  "slug": "token-inspector",
  "name": "Token Inspector",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "Two skills that help you understand and optimize your Claude Code context window. Inspect Context gives you a full token breakdown by source (files, history, skills, MCP configs) with a keep/remove recommendation for each. Find Bloat scans everything loaded and surfaces what's burning tokens without contributing to your current task — with exact commands to remove it.",
  "longDescription": "Ships **8 skills**.\n\n- **Skills** (8): `context-health` (Quick one-liner health check of your context window), `find-bloat` (Find large context items that are not relevant to the current request), `history-trim` (Analyze conversation history turn-by-turn and identify the exact point to run /clear from to prune stale history while…), `inspect-context` (Analyze the current context window and report a breakdown of what's consuming tokens — system prompts, files, conversation…), `mcp-audit` (Audit all connected MCP servers and their tool definitions), `slim-instructions` (Analyze CLAUDE.md and other loaded instruction files for verbosity, redundancy, and bloat), `suggest-split` (Detect when a conversation has drifted across multiple unrelated topics and recommend whether to start a new conversation), `token-forecast` (Estimate how many tokens a file, directory, URL, or pasted content would add to your context before you…)\n\nInstalls with `claude plugin install token-inspector@claude-community` from `msiShariful/claude-token-inspector`.",
  "compatibility": [
    "claude",
    "copilot",
    "antigravity",
    "codex"
  ],
